{
	title: 'Web composer buttons name themselves; desktop captions explain them',
	spec: "Each web composer action button (Pause/Continue, Queue, Steer, Send, Run, Save queued message) shows its name in small caps under its icon. The icon stays the main signal; the name is extra help for those who can read it at that size. On devices with hover and a fine pointer, hovering or keyboard-focusing a button also shows its description under the button row: Steer 'Send message immediately. Interrupts ongoing work.', Queue 'Sent after this turn ends.', and an equally short one for each other button. Touch devices show no caption. Name, caption, aria-label and title come from one source per button, so they never disagree. Buttons keep 44px touch targets; the row does not overflow at 390px wide. The terminal is unchanged: its key hint row already names each action (user decision 2026-10-06).",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['v0g', 'nzv']
}
